# rena0-jump-chain — F1-3 fixture
# Expectations cite FUN_0043ffc0 cases 0x28/0x29/0x2a (the jump chain 40 -> 41 -> 42).
#
# Finding recorded while authoring this fixture: the chain is NOT apex-driven. The port's
# own cited physics (kJumpSpeed 720 u/s, kGravity 1800 u/s^2, kJumpApexSpeed 360;
# fighter.h:283-291) puts the apex at 24 updates, yet the bound set leaves row 40 within
# 4 updates, passes row 41 at 4-6, is on a further chain set by 10 and is on row 42 by 30,
# while the fighter stays airborne through update 47 and lands at 48. So the 40/41/42
# transitions are phase-driven and early relative to the apex, and row 42 covers most of
# the flight. The audit test asserts the same three rows exist but not their timing; these
# anchors are this build's measured trace, and the timing divergence is an open question
# for the seam audit rather than something this fixture settles.
#
# The below-cap start also pins the unified meter's jump economy (V3-9/V3-11): the launch
# tick refills by its row-40 rule, then every climbing tick drains 10 (row 41). The meter,
# not an altitude cap, ends the climb -- the 420-unit kFlyMaxAlt was a port invention and
# no longer applies on the pilot path. No launch spend exists in the jump bodies.
#
# The update-10 link is asserted by raw set index because its row is unresolved here:
# first_set_index(41)=3 and first_set_index(42)=5, so set 4 is a further chain row (the
# audit's allow-list is sets {2,3,4,5,43}) whose move-row identity is not yet identified.
combo 0 0
seed 5489
spawn 0 0 0 0
spawn 1 0 0 2000
collision open-field
charge_gauge 900
input 0 JUMP
input 1 -
expect 0 anim_row 40
expect 24 airborne 1
expect 0 charge_gauge 980
# A one-tick tap releases immediately, so there is no sustained climb: vy decays from the
# leap's 12/tick and the arc lands at 25 (the old 48 came from pinning vy at 12 every tick).
# Holding the button is the case the climb rules below cover -- height is bounded only by
# the meter, never by an altitude cap (V3-11).
expect 4 anim_row 42
expect 10 anim_set 5
expect 20 airborne 1
expect 25 airborne 0
expect 55 dummy_static 1
